    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `checkDigit` as a Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Transient` computed getter `getCheckDigit()` that returns an `Integer` (the standard Luhn check digit, 0\u20139, over the digits in `customerCode`), or `null` when `customerCode` is unset. This matches the existing pattern of derived getters like `getMembershipNumber()` / `getLocality()`, and replicates the exact Luhn algorithm the acceptance test uses.\n\n2. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `checkDigit` read-only integer property (0\u20139) to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` gets the field and MapStruct auto-maps `Owner.getCheckDigit()` into the JSON response.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode`) now passes: it recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and the `checkDigit` field matches exactly.",
