    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe new `getCheckDigit()` slots cleanly into Owner's well-established convention of `@Transient`, Javadoc'd, self-derived getters (`getDisplayName`, `getInitials`, `getMembershipNumber`, `getMembershipLevel`, `getLocality`, `getIdentityKey`, `getContactPreference`). Specifically:\n\n- **Right unit.** The value derives solely from the owner's own `customerCode`, so computing it on the `Owner` entity \u2014 not in a service or helper \u2014 matches how every other derived attribute here is modeled.\n- **Good placement.** It sits immediately after `getMembershipNumber()`, the other `customerCode`-derived getter, grouping the two code-based derivations together.\n- **No duplication.** There's no existing Luhn or digit-folding logic elsewhere to reuse; the loop is self-contained and local to its single use.\n- **Not a catch-all concern.** The class already hosts a family of derived getters by design; this adds one more consistent member rather than bolting on an unrelated responsibility.\n- **Consistent doc + schema.** The Javadoc mirrors the style of its neighbors, and the `openapi.yml` entry (`readOnly`, bounded 0\u20139, example) matches how the other derived, read-only fields are documented.\n\nNo structural changes needed.",
